ile would be a pure-loss refactor across 30 modules.\n\n---\n\n## Then, when convenient\n\n### 4. `src/esbuild/index.ts` — `runEsbuild` 237 lines (`crime_00028`, `crime_00023`, `crime_00092`, `crime_00071`)\n\nThe worst *local* offender: 237 lines at **4.0× the domain threshold**, plus an options bag with **38 distinct property reads** — the largest in the scan by a factor of four. But fan-in is **1** and transitive importers 7, so `blast_radius` is 0.25 and the aggregate `agent_risk` lands at just 0.30/0.36.\n\nThat low fan-in is the reason to do it *fourth* rather than *first*, and also the reason it's pleasant work: one importer means you can restructure aggressively without a coordination cost. Its fan-out 11 (`crime_00092`) is at p99 but is not itself the problem — an esbuild orchestrator importing 11 plugin modules is doing its job.\n\n### 5. `src/index.ts` — 459 lines, fan-out 17 (`crime_00090`, `crime_00054`, `crime_00029/30/31`)\n\nRead the three high-severity `large_function` hits carefully before planning: `build` 167–459, `<anonymous>` 183–456, `mainTasks` 260–453. **These are nested, not three separate functions** — it's one 293-line body with two inner layers. Treat it as a single extraction job (`mainTasks`, `startWatcher` L367–445, `buildAll` L291–365 into their own modules), not three.\n\nFan-out 17 exceeds the p99 cutoff of 11 and is the highest in the repo — but this is the package entry point, and fan-in is only 4 with 7 transitive importers (`blast_radius` 0.28). Extract the god function; do not chase the fan-out number. `crime_00016` (`build` performs `createLogger`/`removeFiles` under a pure-sounding name) resolves naturally during that extraction.\n\n---\n\n## Leave alone\n\n**`schema.json`** (`crime_00088`) — 362 lines, `blast_radius` **0**, `agent_risk` 0.20, no importers. A JSON Schema document is supposed to be one file; `large_file` here is a threshold artifact, not a finding. Suppress it.\n\n**`src/rollup.ts`** (`crime_00069`, `crime_00034`, `crime_00004`, `crime_00070`, `crime_00022`) — this is the clearest \"real problems, zero leverage\" case in the scan. `getRollupConfig` is 122 lines, misleadingly named for something that calls `setSilent` and `removeFiles`, and `runRollup` swallows errors. And **every one of those findings reports `blast_radius` 0, `blast_radius_direct_importers` 0, `blast_radius_transitive_importers` 0** — fan-in is 0. Nothing imports it. Fix opportunistically the next time you're editing the file; never schedule a trip.\n\n**`test/utils.ts`** (`crime_00091`, `crime_00089`) — fan-in 9 looks alarming until you note it's test scaffolding imported by 9 test files, transitive reach 9, and it contains no production code. The unbounded `Promise.all` over `Object.keys(files).map(…)` (confidence 0.88) is genuine but bounded by fixture size — a test-flakiness concern, not a blast-radius one.\n\n**`src/api-extractor.ts`** (`crime_00050`) — fan-out 6 against a p95 cutoff of **6**. It's on the threshold by exactly zero margin, with fan-in 1. Detector noise; ignore the connectivity finding. Its `direct_date` (`crime_00012`) and `swallowed_error` (`crime_00025`) are worth a small pass whenever `src/tsc.ts` gets the identical treatment — the two files carry structurally identical findings (`Date.now()` timing pairs + a catch that logs without the error).\n\n**`src/esbuild/postcss.ts` and `src/esbuild/svelte.ts`** — the `large_function` and `return_shape_roulette` findings here (`crime_00032/33`, `crime_00017/18/19`) are describing the esbuild plugin contract itself: a plugin *is* a name plus a `setup` closure, and `onResolve`/`onLoad` handlers *do* return `{namespace, path}` in one branch and `{contents, loader}` in another. The 0% key overlap is the API's discriminated union, not drift. Add explicit return types if you want the detector quiet; don't restructure.\n\n---\n\n## One caveat on this ranking\n\nEvery finding in this scan reports `churn: 0` and `recency: 0` — there's no git history feeding the scoring, so this is a purely static ranking. Items 3–5 are the ones most likely to reorder under real churn data; if `src/index.ts` turns out to be the file everyone touches weekly, it moves up past `esbuild/index.ts`. Items 1 and 2 won't move — fan-in 18 and fan-in 10 dominate regardless of history.",
